The core features of Vault include:

    Secure Secret Storage: Encrypts secrets at rest.
    Dynamic Secrets: Generates secrets (like database credentials) on the fly with limited lifespans.
    Data Encryption: Encrypts and decrypts data without storing it.
    Access Control: Policies define who can access what.
    Audit Logging: Tracks who accessed which secret and when

What Does It Mean to Unseal Vault?
Vault operates in two states:
    Sealed: Vault is locked and cannot access its encryption keys. No secrets can be read or written.
    Unsealed: Vault has access to its encryption keys and can operate normally.
